<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Janna was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> poet at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veera-ballala-ii">Veera Ballala II</a> and Narasimha II. His best-known works are the Yashodhara Charite of 1209, a Jain moral tale, and the Anantanatha Purana of 1230. He also served as a minister and was honoured with the title Kavichakravarti, emperor among poets.</p></div>
